cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MomentBench: Corpus-Scale Video Moment Retrieval Benchmark"
message: "If you use MomentBench, please cite the version you evaluated on, as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: Mixpeek
    website: https://mixpeek.com
repository-code: https://github.com/mixpeek/momentbench
url: https://github.com/mixpeek/momentbench
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.2.5"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
keywords:
  - video retrieval
  - temporal grounding
  - moment localization
  - benchmark
  - multimodal
  - agentic evaluation
abstract: >-
  MomentBench measures whether a system can find one specific moment, the right
  video and the right few seconds, from a text request, searching a whole corpus
  rather than a single clip. Version 0.2 has 27 hash-verified assets (Blender open
  movies, NASA aerospace video and NASA robotics video, about 117 minutes, public
  domain or CC BY) and 619 queries in four tiers: single-shot visual, dialogue plus
  picture, no-answer near misses, and ordered multi-shot events. 456 queries are
  published and 163 held out; queries on footage newer than current model training
  cutoffs form a rolling split. Queries were drafted and verified by one model,
  cross-checked by a second model family and reviewed frame by frame by a model;
  human review is pending. An agentic track gives models tools to list videos,
  search transcripts and sample frames under a fixed budget, and reports Recall@1
  with bootstrap intervals, net score (a wrong answer costs more than abstaining)
  and cost per query.
